<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίστιον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slip</i> or <i>shed</i> for a
			ship, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆες . . εἰρύαται: πᾶσιν γὰρ
				ἐπίστιόν</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστιν ἑκάστῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.265
				</span></i>
			. (Expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>(ap.Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.125
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἴστιόν . . ὡσεὶ κατάλυμα παρὰ τῇ
				νηΐ</span>) as 
				Ion.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφέστιον</span>, cf. sq.;
			but elsewh. <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always uses the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφέστιος</span>; Sch. has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐποίκιον</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεώριον . . , παρὰ
				τὸ ἱστίον</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
